{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he shall wash his flesh.</b> After he laid his hands on the scapegoat." "<b>And he shall offer his burnt offering.</b> After he has made atonement for himself with his sin offering and for the people with the two sin offerings — for the scapegoat too is called a sin offering, as it says: שְׁנֵי שְׂעִירֵי עִזִּים לְחַטָּאת (Leviticus 16:5). And both of them precede the people's burnt offering, according to the rule of every sin offering, which precedes the burnt offering everywhere, as transmitted in the received tradition." "<b>And he shall make atonement for himself and for the people.</b> The atonement of the thoughts of the heart, which is suited for those of clean hands and pure heart — and this is through the burnt offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:29.999644917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}